From 171bb853fe08a3ec1d2bccfea92fe56d49986631 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PocketForge CI <ci@pocketforge.local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/50] tests: cover A133 SPL CCU pinctrl UART0 and MMC0 gating

Add the pocketforge-a133-ccu qtest for the early CCU/PIO behavior the
pinned A133 SPL relies on: one hermetic invocation carries the full
positive sequence (PLL lock polling at +0x000/+0x020/+0x028, bus factor
words at +0x500/+0x510/+0x51c/+0x520/+0x524/+0x540, UART gate/reset at
+0x90c, MMC clock/gate/reset with +0x84c readback at +0x830/+0x84c, and
the exact legacy-stride PB/PF pinmux RMW cells 0x28/0x40/0xb4/0xc8/0xd0)
plus negative controls that each omit one required gate/reset or pinmux
transition and assert the gated peripheral stays inaccessible: UART0
passes banner bytes to its chardev only after CCU gate/reset AND PB9/PB10
function 2, and the reused A100 SD host receives commands only after CCU
gate/reset AND PF0..PF5 function 2.  Register-level assertions, never a
bare timeout, decide every negative.

The mmio-map test programs the same SPL gate sequence before the flat
view and UART contract probes, and the mmc test performs the SPL MMC0
clock/gate/pinmux sequence before driving the controller, matching the
wiring the model change introduces.

Rebase resolutions:
- Qtest Meson: register the CCU test in the v11 qtests_aarch64 map.

Assisted-by: LLM

